,"created_at":"2026-10-16T20:34:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T18:14:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n-Reproducible in: 4.8.beta 1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.beta1 - Windows 11 (build 26300) - Multi-window, 2 monitors (2560x1440 @ 165.00 Hz, 2880x1620 @ 60.00 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1692) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-12700H (20 threads) - 63.74 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nUpon entering tree, a Trail3D with `limit_mode` set to Length and with non-default `width` or `color` parameters throws the error:\n\n`ERROR: Signal 'frame_pre_draw' is already connected to given callable 'Trail3D::_process_trail' in that object.`\n\non the console, on both the editor and runtime.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add Trail3D node\n2. Set Limit Mode to Length\n3. Change Width or Color property to be any value other than the defaults.\n4. Save Scene.\n5. Reopen Scene.\n\nAlternatively: After step 3, copy the Trail3D node and paste it anywhere, the enter tree notification will trigger the duplicate signal connection and throw the error on the console.\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[trail3d-signal-connect.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33578055/trail3d-signal-connect.zip)\n\n1. Open Trail3D.tscn\n2. Get error on console","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124560/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124560/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,